    description: "Repro: hypergumbo search 'main' --kind nonexistent_kind  # No symbols found, exit 0. Same for --language nonexistent_language, --limit 0, --limit -5. Same fail-silent class as PP (config silently accepts non-language args), QQ (wrong-view JSON), RR (unknown boundary), AA (unknown type). Bundles into the broader input-validation audit PR. Found in dogfooding pass 10 (2026-05-28)."  # 065b
    fields:  # 065b
      statement: "hypergumbo search PATTERN --kind nonexistent_kind returns 'No symbols found' (exit 0) instead of erroring. Same for --language unknown_lang, --limit 0, --limit -5. No validation against the known kind/language vocabulary or limit range."  # 065b
      root_cause: "The search command does not validate --kind / --language values against the actual enum of kinds (function, method, class, file, variable, ...) and languages (python, javascript, ...) present in the behavior_map or analyzer catalog. --limit accepts any int including 0 and negatives. The result is a silent empty response that may mask typos or missing filters in CI scripts."  # 065b
